      "message": "Once this function is called, you are over writing the GPIO settings initialized from the devicetree.  This means `gpio_reset_port()` no longer configures the GPIO pins back to the reset state.\n\nThe caller should provide it\u0027s own array to save the GPIO settings. The caller then passes the array back to `gpio_port_set_config()`. \n\n\nUse `ioex_save/restore_gpio_state()` as a model to follow.\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/common/ioexpander.c;l\u003d158",
